<p>Pope Leo XIV used remarks to reporters on April 18 while flying to Angola to ease the sense of a feud with President Trump. He said he had no interest in debating the US president and that some reporting on his Africa-trip comments had not been accurate in all respects. He added that a speech delivered earlier in Cameroon about a world being &quot;ravaged by a handful of tyrants&quot; had been written well before President Trump’s criticism of him and was not directed at the president. The exchange grew out of Pope Leo’s outspoken emphasis on peace, including criticism of military spending and comments that some coverage linked to tensions with Washington after he spoke out against the Iran war. Even as he tried to cool the dispute, the pope kept his broader message intact, saying his focus during the Africa tour was to preach peace rather than engage in a personal political clash. That shifts attention back to his diplomatic and pastoral agenda on the continent.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ppazeEAJobkjFD2XUdwHXktHFyLwT0-hCJJrt9RM5cpttvZ9K_zfwm9VmoRawvz8eNQUMbFxeo2qovWIwDImWPjA07W8O52mdwA-0-NzCUpZlo4Wu65dP-SN6qxNSEzDNWroMp1tS07ST36g3vTyQ4-uHltzbLhEtpZgKlrHO4EjukJHdjVH74Qaw9ecz7B3qsA0nqOvBIKqojMtNTwh72-jQgFpTAdImeEFZItk7L_ggQOufiGCkghgcPYCsv7cJ5PJgpog0wyFgMhJLA' alt='Pope Leo XIV arrives at the Luanda International Airport in Angola on Saturday, the sixth day of his tour of Africa.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: He said he regretted that people had interpreted his remarks as opening a debate with President Trump, and stressed that he wanted the focus to stay on the peace message he was promoting. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/18/pope-says-he-regrets-his-remarks-interpreted-as-a-debate-with-trump_6752568_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: It described Trump’s attack on Leo at the start of the Africa trip as the moment that prompted a sharper public response from a pope who had previously been seen as cautious. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/18/world/europe/trump-pope-leo-iran.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-plays-down-rift-with-trump-doubles-down-on-peace/a-76842971'>Pope Leo plays down rift with Trump, doubles down on peace</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-pope-leo-downplays-feud-with-trump-says-not-in-my-interest-to-debate/'>Pope Leo downplays feud with Trump, says ‘not in my interest’ to debate him</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/18/world/africa/pope-news-media-trump-africa.html'>Pope Says News Outlets Misread Some of His Remarks as Criticism of Trump</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350604/pope-leo-seeks-defuse-tensions-trump-says-not-trying-debate-him'>Pope Leo seeks to defuse tensions with Trump, says not trying to debate him</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce84j261kj1o'>Pope says &#x27;tyrants&#x27; speech was not aimed at Trump</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/pope-leo-says-not-trying-debate-trump-preach-peace-africa/'>Pope Leo says he is not trying to debate Trump, but preach peace in Africa</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/18/pope-says-he-regrets-his-remarks-interpreted-as-a-debate-with-trump_6752568_4.html'>Pope says he regrets his remarks interpreted as a debate with Trump</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>